{%- doc -%}
  Renders one of the theme's decorative background shapes: an organic blob that sits behind a
  photo. Purely decorative, so it is hidden from assistive technology and takes no focus.

  Every shape here is lifted verbatim from the legacy section that draws it today -- same
  viewBox, same intrinsic size, same path data, same colour -- so a converted section looks the
  same as the one it replaces. `tests/decorative-shape.test.mjs` compares each one against its
  source file and fails on any drift, which is why none of this should be edited by hand.

  The intrinsic size matters and is easy to lose. An inline `<svg>` with only a viewBox is a
  replaced element with a default 300px width, and `max-width` caps it rather than stretching
  it -- so dropping the `width`/`height` the careers and training shapes carry would shrink
  them from 457px and 477px to about 300px against a photo that stretches to its container.
  Two of the six have those attributes and four do not; both states are reproduced, because
  either one is what its section draws today.

  Despite the legacy class name `animated-svg`, nothing animates: `.start`, `.medium` and
  `.end` have no rule in any stylesheet and no script touches them, so all three paths paint in
  one colour and what the page shows is their union.

  @param {string} shape - one of: sourcing, about, awards, careers, training, enquiry
  @param {string} [color] - overrides the shape's own fill
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign shape_width = blank
  assign shape_height = blank

  case shape
    when 'sourcing'
      assign view_box = '0 0 402.06 268.72'
      assign shape_fill = '#dfa46d'
    when 'about'
      assign view_box = '0 0 462.1 372.8'
      assign shape_fill = '#BDD6E6'
    when 'awards'
      assign view_box = '0 0 462.1 372.8'
      assign shape_fill = '#BDD6E6'
    when 'careers'
      assign view_box = '0 0 457 372'
      assign shape_fill = '#D0994D'
      assign shape_width = '457'
      assign shape_height = '372'
    when 'training'
      assign view_box = '0 0 477 428'
      assign shape_fill = '#D0994D'
      assign shape_width = '477'
      assign shape_height = '428'
    when 'enquiry'
      assign view_box = '0 0 823.5 736.6'
      assign shape_fill = '#BDD6E6'
    else
      assign view_box = blank
  endcase

  if color != blank
    assign shape_fill = color
  endif
-%}

